# cloudflared-specific NON-SECRET config. This file IS committed.
#
# Shared values (PUID/PGID/TZ/CONFIG_ROOT/DATA_ROOT) live in ../../common.env.
#
# TUNNEL_TOKEN is deliberately NOT here — it is a secret. It comes from the
# Komodo Variable CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN (Settings > Variables, "Secret" enabled),
# interpolated into the generated komodo.env at deploy time via the
# `environment` field on the stack in komodo/resources/stacks.toml.
#
# The tunnel token grants the ability to route traffic into this network, so
# it belongs in the same tier as any other credential: never in git.

# Nothing cloudflared-specific needed yet.
